# Environment variable reference. Configure Nullius through Settings,
# which saves to your user settings.json, or export variables for automation.
# Existing app/.env files can be imported with nullius migrate --from CHECKOUT.
# Process environment variables win over saved settings. Never commit secrets.

# Start-up options, not on the Settings page:
#   NULLIUS_HOME: a separate profile with config/, data/ and cache/ directories
#   NULLIUS_CATALOGUE: the user catalogue directory (default catalogue/ in the user data directory)
#   NULLIUS_PRICES: the model price list file (default prices.json in the user configuration directory); set for a run on a host
#   APP_HOST: the address the server binds (default 127.0.0.1, or --host)
#   APP_PORT: the port the server listens on (default 5057, or --port)
#   JOB_ROOTS: job roots to open at start (or the command-line argument)
#   WORKSPACES_DIR: where workspaces are kept (default workspaces/ in the user data directory)
#   WORKSPACE: the name the start-up roots open as (or the picker's name field)
#   DATASET_ROOTS: local dataset checkouts to look in for task files
#   DEBUG: the Werkzeug debugger (or --no-debug)
#   RUNS_DIR: where runs started from the builder keep their script, log and job (default runs/ in the user data directory)
#   HARBOR_PINS: where the Harbor a recipe pins is built and kept on this machine (default harbor-pins/ beside the runs)
#   STANDARD_DIR: where the Nullius standard installs agents, capabilities and benchmark upstreams (default standard/ in the user data directory)
#   STANDARD_DATA_DIR: where the Nullius standard keeps the datasets it downloads, which can be gigabytes (default datasets/ in STANDARD_DIR)
#   SECRETS_DIR: where each benchmark's licences (Settings → Custom keys) and the Hugging Face token (Settings → Data providers) are kept (default secrets/ in the user configuration directory)

# --- Model credentials ---
# The key of the OpenAI-compatible endpoint at MODEL_API_URL: a recipe on that endpoint is sent there with this key. Optional, for a server that checks none: without it the run is sent the word 'local' as its key. A run gets it as API_TOKEN, OPENAI_API_KEY and LLM_API_KEY in its environment - over stdin to a host - and never in a recipe or a log.
#   e.g. sk-…
MODEL_API_KEY=
# The URL of an OpenAI-compatible endpoint, API path included, required for a recipe on it: there is no default to fall back on, and the builder offers the endpoint only once it is set. It is shown on the page, so it holds no credential: no user or password, no key in its query. More endpoints, each with a name, are MODEL_<ID>_NAME, MODEL_<ID>_API_URL and MODEL_<ID>_API_KEY. A run gets it as API_URL, OPENAI_BASE_URL and LLM_BASE_URL.
#   e.g. https://…/v1
MODEL_API_URL=
# An OpenAI key, for a recipe whose provider is OpenAI: that run is sent to OpenAI's own endpoint, https://api.openai.com/v1, with this key - never with the model API key or its endpoint. It reaches the run as the model key does, and never a recipe or a log.
OPENAI_API_KEY=
# An OpenRouter key, for a recipe whose provider is OpenRouter: that run is sent to OpenRouter's own endpoint, https://openrouter.ai/api/v1, with this key - never with the model API key or its endpoint. It reaches the run as the model key does, and never a recipe or a log.
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
# An Anthropic key, for a run of the Nullius standard whose provider is Anthropic: its relay sends the calls to Anthropic's own endpoint, https://api.anthropic.com/v1, with this key. Only the relay holds it - never an agent, a recipe or a log.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# TypeSafe.ai key for the System One judgement on TypeSafe's own endpoint, POST https://api.typesafe.ai/v1/systemone — sent as a bearer header there and nowhere else.
#   e.g. ts-…
TYPESAFE_API_KEY=
# Where the System One judgement is asked: typesafe (its own endpoint, with TYPESAFE_API_KEY) or openrouter (https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/systemone, the same contract, with OPENROUTER_API_KEY). Unset: TypeSafe when its key is set, else OpenRouter when its key is.
SYSTEM_ONE_PROVIDER=
# The System One model, as the provider names it: on TypeSafe jev-latest, on OpenRouter ~typesafe/jev-latest, typesafe/jev-router, jaredpalmer/kev-4b... Unset: the provider's Jev.
SYSTEM_ONE_MODEL=
# The provider of the LLM judgement, the second judgement beside System One: openrouter, openai, local (the endpoint at MODEL_API_URL) or local:<ID> (the endpoint MODEL_<ID>_API_URL), asked with that provider's own key and endpoint from the model providers above. Unset: the first of them that is set.
LLM_JUDGE_PROVIDER=
# The model of the LLM judgement, as its provider names it (on OpenRouter, vendor/model). It is asked the same questions as System One and answers them as JSON; its numbers are what it states, so a choice or a score carries no confidence.
LLM_JUDGE_MODEL=

# --- Run hosts ---
# Machines a recipe can run on, over ssh: an alias from ~/.ssh/config, or user@host[:port][:/path/to/key]. Only the name is stored; keys stay where they are.
#   e.g. user@host[:port][:/path/to/key]
HOSTS=

# --- Custom keys ---
# The names of the agent keys this file holds, comma-separated: the keys an agent needs of its own vendor, beside the model's (Cursor's CLI agent a CURSOR_API_KEY, Copilot's a GH_TOKEN). Each is a line of its own in this file. A Harbor run gets every one of them in its environment - over stdin to a host - and a Nullius standard run's never; none is ever written into a recipe or a log.
AGENT_KEYS=
